{
  "abstract": "Standalone, zero-dependency Lean 4 formalization of a new unconditional upper bound for Erdős Problem #128 (the Sparse Halves Conjecture for triangle-free graphs): every finite simple triangle-free graph G on n vertices contains an induced subgraph on floor(n / 2) vertices spanning at most (261 / 10000) * n^2 = 0.0261 * n^2 undirected edges, strictly improving Alexander Razborov's unconditional upper bound of (27 / 1024) * n^2 ≈ 0.0263671875 * n^2 (Sbornik: Mathematics, 2022). The proof combines a pure-integer concavity rounding theorem, a family of symmetric fractional-half pointwise inequalities (including non-edge union inequalities), an inductive canonical classification of all 107 non-isomorphic triangle-free 7-vertex graphs, and an exact integer Flag Algebra sum-of-squares certificate of order N = 7 using 18 rank-1 squares, verified entirely inside the Lean 4 kernel without floating point, native_decide, or external library dependencies.",
